# Copy to .env.local for development. Never commit .env.local.
# In production these live in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=https://jaynguyen.fyi

# --- Phase 2: Payload CMS -------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URI=postgresql://user:pass@host/db?sslmode=require
# PAYLOAD_SECRET=            # openssl rand -base64 32

# --- Phase 2: media storage ----------------------------------------------
# Vercel Blob, injected automatically by Vercel in production.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_...

# --- Phase 7: contact form -----------------------------------------------
# Get a key at resend.com. Without it the form still works: messages are
# stored in Postgres and readable in /admin, and the row records that no
# notification email went out. That is the intended degraded mode, not a bug.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#
# MUST be an address on a domain verified in Resend — jaynguyen.fyi, once its
# DNS records are added there. Do NOT set this to the visitor's address or to
# a gmail.com address you do not control: it will fail SPF/DKIM alignment and
# land in spam. The visitor goes in reply_to instead, so Reply still works.
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=Portfolio <contact@jaynguyen.fyi>
#
# The recipient is NOT configured here — it is the email in Site Settings, so
# changing where messages land is an edit in /admin rather than a redeploy.
